{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What grace, O Lord, and beauty shone
\par Around Thy steps below;
\par What patient love was seen in all
\par Thy life and death of woe!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For ever on Thy burdened heart
\par A weight of sorrow hung,
\par Yet no ungentle, murmuring word
\par Escaped Thy silent tongue.
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy foes might hate, despise, revile,
\par Thy friends unfaithful prove,
\par Unwearied in forgiveness still,
\par Thy heart could only love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O give us hearts to love like Thee,
\par Like Thee, O Lord, to grieve
\par Far more for others' sins, than all
\par The wrongs that we receive.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. One with Thyself, may every eye
\par In us, Thy  brethren, see
\par the gentleness and grace that spring
\par from union, Lord, with Thee.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

